  "instruction": "out of the artists who participated in the 2023 The Art of Texas State Parks traveling art exhibit, which ones were from austin texas?",
  "answer": "Based on the deep research across multiple official sources (TPWD press releases, Bullock Museum pages, Texas A&M Press catalog, and news coverage), **four artists** from the 2023 \"The Art of Texas State Parks\" traveling exhibit were from Austin, Texas:\n\n## Austin-Based Artists in the 2023 Exhibit\n\n| Artist | Notes |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Fidencio Duran** | Austin-based painter & muralist; painted LBJ State Park (Sauer-Beckmann Living History Farm) |\n| **Malou Flato** | Longtime Austin resident with studio in Austin + Hill Country ranch; painted Pedernales Falls State Park |\n| **Gordon Fowler** | Native Texan, Austin-based 50+ years; taught watercolor at UT & The Contemporary Austin; painted Bastrop State Park and Honey Creek State Natural Area |\n| **Terri M. Wells** | Listed as Austin-based in TPWD/CBS Austin rosters |\n\n## Sources\n1. TPWD Official Press Release (Jan 3, 2023) — https://tpwd.texas.gov/newsmedia/releases?req=20230103a\n2. TPWD Official Press Release (Oct 26, 2023) — https://tpwd.texas.gov/newsmedia/releases?req=20231026a\n3. Bullock Texas State History Museum exhibit page — https://www.thestoryoftexas.com/special-exhibits/art-of-the-texas-parks\n4. Texas A&M University Press book catalog — https://www.tamupress.com/book/9781648430688/the-art-of-texas-state-parks\n5. Texas Monthly feature — https://www.texasmonthly.com/arts-entertainment/bullock-museum-texas-state-parks-centennial\n6. TPW Magazine (Jan/Feb 2023) — https://tpwmagazine.com/parks/artists-celebrate-the-100th-anniversary-of-texas-state-parks\n7. Glasstire coverage — https://glasstire.com/2023/01/13/state-park-art-exhibit-to-travel-texas\n\nAll four Austin artists were part of the 30-artist cohort commissioned for the centennial celebration, creating works across 65+ Texas state parks.",
